nslate(30, 175)'><rect x='0' y='0' width='900' height='100' rx='8' fill='#f8fafc' stroke='#cbd5e1'/><text x='15' y='22' font-family='Arial' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' fill='#0369a1'>Why Formaldehyde is Exclusively Oxidized:</text><text x='15' y='42' font-family='Arial' font-size='11' fill='#334155'>1. Steric Accessibility: Unhindered C=O allows extremely fast OH− attack compared to bulky ArCHO.</text><text x='15' y='60' font-family='Arial' font-size='11' fill='#334155'>2. Electronic Effect: Absence of electron-donating aryl ring makes HCHO carbon much more electrophilic.</text><text x='15' y='78' font-family='Arial' font-size='11' fill='#334155'>3. Synthetic Utility: Quantitative conversion of valuable aldehydes into primary alcohols without loss to carboxylate side-products.</text></g></g></svg></div>"
